    "title": "PBS Preview Screening with Director Lynn Novick, Rahsaan Thomas, and Guests",
    "description": "What does justice truly mean in America?\n\nJoin acclaimed filmmaker Lynn Novick for an exclusive preview screening of her forthcoming PBS documentary, Crime and Punishment in America (executive produced by Ken Burns), co-presented by The Commonwealth Club World Affairs.\n\nFollowing the screening, Novick will be joined for a vital panel conversation by consulting producer Rahsaan Thomas (former co-host of the Peabody Award-winning podcast Ear Hustle and Executive Director of Empowerment Avenue), correctional wellness advocate Stephen B. Walker, and survivor advocate Jess Nichol. Together, they will unpack the four-century history of criminal justice in America and explore how our nation has grappled with crime, punishment, and accountability.\n\nEvent Details:\n🗓 Date: Tuesday, October 27, 2026\n🕕 Schedule: 6:00 PM Screening | 7:00 PM Conversation\n📍 Location: Commonwealth Club World Affairs, 312 Sutter St #200, San Francisco, CA 94108\n🎟 Tickets: $22 (In-person only — no livestream available)\n\nSeats are limited. Secure your tickets, link in bio.\n\n#CrimeAndPunishmentInAmerica #PBS #LynnNovick #KenBurns #RahsaanThomas #EarHustle #CriminalJustice #DocumentaryFilm #SanFranciscoEvents #CommonwealthClub #SFEvents #SocialJustice\n\n@kqed @cinemas_sf @loscenzontles @jimmyjames",
