    "title": "Scaling Intelligence: Modal x Gray Area AI Commissions",
    "description": "What happens when artists get access to compute at the scale industry runs on?\n\nScaling Intelligence: Modal x Gray Area AI Commissions opens Wednesday, October 28 at Gray Area. 13 artists debut new work built with AI and large-scale cloud computing, moving between scales that rarely meet: a satellite’s planetary view beside a microbial colony, the inside of a neural network opening onto forests and watersheds, a day of visitor conversation becoming a creature’s memory.\n\nRather than using AI to make more of the same, these artists treat it as a translation layer, letting intelligences of vastly different sizes and speeds sense one another.\n\nOf those 13 artists, Ira Greenberg (@greenberg.ira) presents Protobyte Phylogeny, a living ecosystem of artificial organisms evolving in real time. Evolve your own specimen at the bench and the population at the close of the show will be partly descended from you.\n\nStop by and become part of the ecosystem!\n\n🌐 Opening Night\nWednesday, Oct 28, 7-10 PM\nRSVP: link in bio\n\n🕑 Exhibition Hours\nThu, Oct 29: 2-6 PM\nFri, Oct 30: 2-8 PM\nSat, Oct 31: 1-8 PM\nSun, Nov 1: 1-8 PM\nVisit: link in bio\n\n📍Gray Area, 2665 Mission St, San Francisco\nFree admission, donations welcome",
