    "title": "SACHI Annual Event: Curator Talk: Vishnu's Cosmic Ocean",
    "description": "On Sunday, November 1, step into the calm and chaos of \"Vishnu’s Cosmic Ocean\"! Join us for the SACHI (Society for Art & Cultural Heritage of India) Annual Event, featuring a rare double-feature talk to celebrate the opening of Southeast Asia’s largest ancient bronze—a breathtaking 1,000-year-old Reclining Vishnu on special loan from the National Museum of Cambodia. \n\nIn this special program presented by SACHI, Asian Art Museum curator Natasha Reichle and curator emeritus Forrest McGill dive into how ancient Cambodian rulers harnessed massive water engineering works and cosmic Hindu myths to display their power, bring prosperity, and inspire grand traditions that endure today.\n\nLink in bio to learn more.",
