    "title": "Presidio Habitat Stewards (weekly)",
    "description": "Every Saturday - and every first and third Wednesday - something quiet and remarkable happens at the Presidio. \n\nStrangers show up. From across the Bay, from different neighborhoods, different backgrounds, different reasons for being here. Most of them don't know each other. But they have one thing in common: they love this place and they want to take care of it.\n\nTogether they pull invasive plants, restore native habitats, and help bring back the forests, wildflowers, and wetlands that make the Presidio one of the most biologically diverse national park sites in the country. \n\nYou won't read about them in the headlines. But walk these trails through the wildflowers, past the wetlands, under the canopy of a forest slowly becoming what it was always meant to be, and you are walking through their work.\n\nNearly three decades of this. Park ecologists and volunteers, side by side, quietly doing the work the rest of us get to enjoy.\n\nWant to be part of it? No experience needed. Just show up, get your hands dirty, and spend a few hours outside in one of the most extraordinary places in California doing something that genuinely matters.\n\nLink in our bio.",
